From: stew675 <stew675@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:34:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip/prefill-decode-arms: landmine 3 CONFIRMED as the two
 allocation cursors, and the fix is one allocator (prefill reserves, decode
 consumes)

ARMS_RESET_CACHE=1 wipes the cell metadata and both per-context cursors at each rep boundary.  With that, the
first request is byte-identical to the single-context reference in every rep, on both the host tier (arena 5000)
and at full residency, and the second request's residual difference collapses into one stable value (rep 1 ==
rep 2).  So the carrier of the warm-rep divergence is the two independent v_heads cursors over the shared cells
-- the same defect class as the double-allocation hazard.

Design instruction recorded: one allocator for the co-owner pair.  The PREFILL arm reserves a slot's cell run at
the handover and publishes it; the DECODE arm consumes the reservation and never searches or advances the shared
cursor (llama_kv_cache::state_read_sinfo(..., sinfos_in) is the existing machinery for a caller-chosen layout).
The take is NOT the setup: it moves the recurrent rows and touches no KV cell, so moving it to the prefill
thread alone changes nothing -- but with a reservation the decode arm does no allocation at all, so there is no
lock on its hot path (a direct mutex take starves the prefill for 2.85 s).  Residual: the second concurrent slot
is now deterministic but still different warm; the next instrument is printing the cell indices per request.
